&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
Server Infrastructure is a Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) team responsible for the full lifecycle of Nebius Cloud hardware: from newly delivered bare metal through provisioning, operation, maintenance, and decommissioning. Almost every Nebius service runs on servers within our domain. Our mission is to make the hardware layer fast, reliable, and invisible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We apply software engineering to infrastructure operations. We build services and automation that bring servers into the cloud, keep them healthy, recover them from failures, and retire them safely. Our work spans CPU and GPU platforms, the base GNU/Linux system, and the infrastructure supporting our hardware fleet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Senior / Staff Engineer, you’ll take ownership of complex infrastructure challenges and help shape the team’s technical direction. You’ll combine hands-on engineering with architecture, mentoring, and coordination across teams, turning operational needs into reliable services and automation.&lt;br&gt;You’ll work closely with data center engineers, capacity managers, cloud compute developers, networking teams, and hardware suppliers. Your work will directly affect the reliability and capacity of the entire cloud platform.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Y&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;our responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate services for netboot, provisioning, maintenance, automated recovery, and decommissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical initiatives from problem definition and design through implementation and production operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the technical roadmap, balancing reliability improvements, new hardware integration, and long-term engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define meaningful reliability indicators and service level objectives, using them to guide engineering priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce operational toil by turning recurring failures and manual procedures into reliable automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve on-call practices, incident response, and learning through blameless incident reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen fleet observability, alerting, testing, deployment safety, and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive support for new CPU and GPU platforms and improvements to the base GNU/Linux system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, provide thoughtful design and code reviews, and help the team develop sound engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate delivery across teams, communicate technical tradeoffs, and resolve dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering experience in Go and a solid understanding of Linux systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, building, and operating infrastructure services, including distributed systems and failure handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning complex technical initiatives and bringing them into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of SRE principles: service level objectives, observability, incident management, capacity planning, and toil reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound technical judgment and the ability to guide architecture and investigate difficult production problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers and improving engineering practices through collaboration and technical example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and the ability to work effectively across engineering and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;We welcome candidates at senior and staff levels. The scope of ownership and technical influence will reflect your experience.&lt;br&gt;Experience with hardware provisioning, &lt;strong&gt;bare metal infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;GPU platforms&lt;/strong&gt;, or large server fleets would be valuable.&lt;br&gt;Familiarity with &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes, infrastructure as code, GitOps, SaltStack, and Terraform&lt;/strong&gt; is also useful.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;We conduct coding interviews as part of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
